<Folder><name>Day 1 · Wed 25 Nov · Arrive Osaka</name>
<Placemark><name>D1.1+2 Fly Hyderabad → Hong Kong → Osaka</name><styleUrl>#d0</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>02:05–15:10</b> Fly Hyderabad → Hong Kong → Osaka (KIX)<br>CX672 lands HKG 09:55, CX506 leaves 10:45.<br>Cost: In package: flights<br><b>⚠ Only 50 minutes to connect in Hong Kong. Bags are checked through, but if the first flight is late you'd be rebooked onto a later flight.</b><br><br><b>15:10–16:20</b> Immigration and bags<br>With Visit Japan Web QR codes this is usually 45–70 min.<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kansai%20International%20Airport">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcOeQvstZTl/">@duoonleave</a> – Visit Japan Web QR codes to skip the immigration queue<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbixvvZtE-4/">@kiram.sb</a> – 5 things to know: Tabelog, Kuli Kuli, Visit Japan Web, carry cash, bins are rare<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kansai_International_Airport">Kansai International Airport (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.244,34.4347,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D1.3 Check in</name><styleUrl>#d0</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>17:15–18:00</b> Check in, S Presso Namba Parks Street<br>Cost: In package, with breakfast<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=34.66%2C135.501">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Namba">Namba (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.501,34.66,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D1.4 Dotonbori and Hozenji Yokocho</name><styleUrl>#d0</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>18:15–21:00</b> Dotonbori and Hozenji Yokocho<br>Glico sign, canal walk, takoyaki, first dinner. Keep it light after a night flight.<br>Cost: You pay: dinner<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dotonbori%2C%20Osaka">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C5%8Dtonbori">Dōtonbori (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.5013,34.6687,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 1 route</name><styleUrl>#d0</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Kansai%20International%20Airport/34.66%2C135.501/Dotonbori%2C%20Osaka">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>135.244,34.4347,0 135.501,34.66,0 135.5013,34.6687,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 2 · Thu 26 Nov · Osaka Pass day</name>
<Placemark><name>D2.1+2 Osaka Castle and park</name><styleUrl>#d1</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>09:00–11:30</b> Osaka Castle and park<br>Go early before tour groups arrive.<br>Cost: Park free; castle tower ~¥1,200, not in the pass<br><br><b>11:30–12:30</b> Osaka Wonder Cruise<br>The departure pier is printed on your voucher; allow 20 min to get there.<br>Cost: In package<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Osaka%20Castle">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osaka_Castle">Osaka Castle (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.5262,34.6873,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D2.3 Lunch</name><styleUrl>#d1</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>13:00–17:30</b> Lunch, then Amerikamura thrift and vintage shops<br>Plus Shinsaibashi-suji covered arcade. All walkable.<br>Cost: You pay: lunch, shopping<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Amerikamura%2C%20Osaka">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dc-vVNATzF8/">@asukunavi.travel</a> – Amerikamura vintage and thrift shopping, Osaka<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amerikamura">Amerikamura (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.4985,34.6722,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D2.4 Dinner around Namba / Ura-Namba</name><styleUrl>#d1</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>18:00–21:00</b> Dinner around Namba / Ura-Namba<br>Use Tabelog: 3.5+ is very good.<br>Cost: You pay: dinner<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dotonbori%2C%20Osaka">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C5%8Dtonbori">Dōtonbori (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.5013,34.6687,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 2 route</name><styleUrl>#d1</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Osaka%20Castle/Amerikamura%2C%20Osaka/Dotonbori%2C%20Osaka">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>135.5262,34.6873,0 135.4985,34.6722,0 135.5013,34.6687,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 3 · Fri 27 Nov · Nara</name>
<Placemark><name>D3.1 Nara Park deer and Kofuku-ji pagoda</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>09:05–09:40</b> Nara Park deer and Kofuku-ji pagoda<br>Deer crackers about ¥200.<br>Cost: Free (museum hall optional ~¥700)<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kofuku-ji%2C%20Nara">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbIUswQyFw6/">@giashn</a> – Nara one-day route: Kasuga Taisha, Mizuya Chaya, Todai-ji, mochi, Wakakusa sunset<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K%C5%8Dfuku-ji">Kōfuku-ji (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.8318,34.683,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D3.2 Kasuga Taisha + water fortune at Meoto Daikokusha</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>10:00–11:10</b> Kasuga Taisha + water fortune at Meoto Daikokusha<br>Cost: Grounds free; inner area ~¥700<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kasuga%20Taisha%2C%20Nara">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbIUswQyFw6/">@giashn</a> – Nara one-day route: Kasuga Taisha, Mizuya Chaya, Todai-ji, mochi, Wakakusa sunset<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kasuga-taisha">Kasuga-taisha (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.8484,34.6812,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D3.3 Lunch</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>11:20–12:05</b> Lunch: handmade udon at Mizuya Chaya<br>Cost: You pay: lunch ~¥1,200<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mizuya%20Chaya%2C%20Nara">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbIUswQyFw6/">@giashn</a> – Nara one-day route: Kasuga Taisha, Mizuya Chaya, Todai-ji, mochi, Wakakusa sunset<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nara_Park">Nara Park (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.847,34.6862,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D3.4 Todai-ji</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>12:15–13:30</b> Todai-ji: Great Buddha, the pillar 'nostril' crawl<br>Cost: ~¥800<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Todai-ji%2C%20Nara">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbIUswQyFw6/">@giashn</a> – Nara one-day route: Kasuga Taisha, Mizuya Chaya, Todai-ji, mochi, Wakakusa sunset<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbcW3kJy4gR/">@giashn</a> – Mt Wakakusa by the Hilltop Bus, Nara<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C5%8Ddai-ji">Tōdai-ji (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.8398,34.689,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D3.5 Nigatsudo balcony view</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>13:30–14:00</b> Nigatsudo balcony view<br>This is also the sunset backup if Mt Wakakusa is closed.<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nigatsu-do%2C%20Nara">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbIUswQyFw6/">@giashn</a> – Nara one-day route: Kasuga Taisha, Mizuya Chaya, Todai-ji, mochi, Wakakusa sunset<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nigatsu-d%C5%8D">Nigatsu-dō (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.8446,34.6895,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D3.6 Mochi-pounding at Nakatanidou</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>14:20–15:50</b> Mochi-pounding at Nakatanidou, Daibutsu pudding at Kintetsu station<br>Rest and snacks before the sunset bus.<br>Cost: You pay: snacks<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nakatanidou%2C%20Nara">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbIUswQyFw6/">@giashn</a> – Nara one-day route: Kasuga Taisha, Mizuya Chaya, Todai-ji, mochi, Wakakusa sunset<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochi">Mochi (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.8296,34.6818,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D3.7 Sunset from Mt Wakakusa</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>16:35–17:10</b> Sunset from Mt Wakakusa (sunset ≈ 16:50)<br>Cost: Free from the bus stop<br><b>⚠ At risk. One listing says the bus season ends 23 Nov, and a source says the hill closes from 24 Nov. Also, the walking path down closes at 17:00, so ride the bus back rather than walking. Check before booking; if it's off, watch sunset from Nigatsudo instead.</b><br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mount%20Wakakusa%2C%20Nara">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbcW3kJy4gR/">@giashn</a> – Mt Wakakusa by the Hilltop Bus, Nara<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbIUswQyFw6/">@giashn</a> – Nara one-day route: Kasuga Taisha, Mizuya Chaya, Todai-ji, mochi, Wakakusa sunset<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Wakakusa">Mount Wakakusa (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.8566,34.6955,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D3.8 Dinner in Namba; pack for Kyoto</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>18:30–21:00</b> Dinner in Namba; pack for Kyoto<br>Send big bags to the Kyoto hotel tonight through the front desk.<br>Cost: You pay: luggage forwarding ~¥2,000 per bag<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dotonbori%2C%20Osaka">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C5%8Dtonbori">Dōtonbori (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.5013,34.6687,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 3 route</name><styleUrl>#d2</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Kofuku-ji%2C%20Nara/Kasuga%20Taisha%2C%20Nara/Mizuya%20Chaya%2C%20Nara/Todai-ji%2C%20Nara/Nigatsu-do%2C%20Nara/Nakatanidou%2C%20Nara/Mount%20Wakakusa%2C%20Nara/Dotonbori%2C%20Osaka">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>135.8318,34.683,0 135.8484,34.6812,0 135.847,34.6862,0 135.8398,34.689,0 135.8446,34.6895,0 135.8296,34.6818,0 135.8566,34.6955,0 135.5013,34.6687,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 4 · Sat 28 Nov · Kyoto east</name>
<Placemark><name>D4.1 Fushimi Inari</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>08:20–10:20</b> Fushimi Inari: torii tunnels up to the Yotsutsuji viewpoint<br>Saturday in peak leaf season: by 10:00 the lower path is packed.<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Fushimi%20Inari%20Taisha">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fushimi_Inari-taisha">Fushimi Inari-taisha (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.7727,34.9671,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D4.2 Kiyomizu-dera</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>10:45–12:00</b> Kiyomizu-dera (autumn leaves at their peak)<br>Cost: ~¥500<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kiyomizu-dera">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiyomizu-dera">Kiyomizu-dera (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.785,34.9949,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D4.3 Yasaka pagoda photo + lunch nearby</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>12:15–13:30</b> Yasaka pagoda photo + lunch nearby<br>Cost: You pay: lunch<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yasaka%20Pagoda%20Hokan-ji%2C%20Kyoto">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yasaka_Pagoda">Yasaka Pagoda (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.7793,34.9985,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D4.4 Yasaka Shrine</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>13:40–14:15</b> Yasaka Shrine<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yasaka%20Shrine%2C%20Kyoto">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yasaka_Shrine">Yasaka Shrine (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.7785,35.0037,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D4.5 Gion</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>14:20–15:10</b> Gion, Hanamikoji street<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hanamikoji%20Street%2C%20Kyoto">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gion">Gion (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.7752,35.0025,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D4.6 Nishiki Market</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>15:25–16:25</b> Nishiki Market<br>Stalls start closing around 17:00.<br>Cost: You pay: tasting<br><b>⚠ Today is overloaded. Better: move Nishiki Market to the evening of Day 5.</b><br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nishiki%20Market%2C%20Kyoto">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nishiki_Market">Nishiki Market (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.765,35.005,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D4.7 Check in</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>16:45–17:30</b> Check in, Kyoto hotel near the station, short rest<br>Cost: Not in quote: 2 nights to add<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kyoto%20Station">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dep4Xv2IPc3/">@tyler.travelssmart</a> – Train money tips: Tokyo 72 h subway ticket, local train Osaka–Kyoto, skip the JR Pass<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ky%C5%8Dto_Station">Kyōto Station (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.7588,34.9858,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D4.8 Eikando autumn night light-up</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>18:00–19:45</b> Eikando autumn night light-up<br>Cost: ~¥1,000 (separate from day entry)<br><b>⚠ Saturday at peak: expect a 30–60 min queue. With Fushimi Inari and Kiyomizu earlier, this day is about 20,000 steps. Choose: drop Nishiki Market, or do Eikando on Sunday night instead.</b><br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Eikando%20Zenrinji%2C%20Kyoto">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DeOD8Tzks5Q/">@photo post</a> – Best autumn-leaf spots in Japan, incl. Arashiyama and Eikando<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eikan-d%C5%8D_Zenrin-ji">Eikan-dō Zenrin-ji (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.794,35.0148,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 4 route</name><styleUrl>#d3</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Fushimi%20Inari%20Taisha/Kiyomizu-dera/Yasaka%20Pagoda%20Hokan-ji%2C%20Kyoto/Yasaka%20Shrine%2C%20Kyoto/Hanamikoji%20Street%2C%20Kyoto/Nishiki%20Market%2C%20Kyoto/Kyoto%20Station/Eikando%20Zenrinji%2C%20Kyoto">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>135.7727,34.9671,0 135.785,34.9949,0 135.7793,34.9985,0 135.7785,35.0037,0 135.7752,35.0025,0 135.765,35.005,0 135.7588,34.9858,0 135.794,35.0148,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 5 · Sun 29 Nov · Arashiyama</name>
<Placemark><name>D5.1 Torokko Saga station</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>08:35–09:01</b> Torokko Saga station: collect Sagano train tickets<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Torokko%20Saga%20Station%2C%20Kyoto">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbaT9dGywsB/">@giashn</a> – Arashiyama day: Sagano Romantic Train + Hozugawa boat + bamboo<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sagano_Scenic_Railway">Sagano Scenic Railway (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.6815,35.018,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D5.2 Torokko Kameoka</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>09:26–10:00</b> Torokko Kameoka: tanuki statues, coffee<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Torokko%20Kameoka%20Station">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbaT9dGywsB/">@giashn</a> – Arashiyama day: Sagano Romantic Train + Hozugawa boat + bamboo<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kameoka%2C_Kyoto">Kameoka, Kyoto (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.6063,35.0198,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D5.3 Hozugawa boat check-in</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>10:15–11:00</b> Hozugawa boat check-in<br>Arrive 30+ min early; the 11:00 boat is what the reel used.<br>Cost: —<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hozugawa%20River%20Boat%20Ride%2C%20Kameoka">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbaT9dGywsB/">@giashn</a> – Arashiyama day: Sagano Romantic Train + Hozugawa boat + bamboo<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hozu_River">Hozu River (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.5862,35.0128,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D5.4 Lunch + cloud matcha at Kumonocha</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>12:45–13:45</b> Lunch + cloud matcha at Kumonocha, Arashiyama<br>Cost: You pay: lunch<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kumonocha%20Cafe%20Arashiyama">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcCY-QOPNlr/">@jessiejanedaye</a> – Food worth the hype: Kumonocha cloud matcha, Age.3 sandos, Hiiragi shaved ice<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arashiyama">Arashiyama (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.6772,35.015,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D5.5 Bamboo grove</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>13:50–14:40</b> Bamboo grove (+ Tenryu-ji garden if time)<br>Cost: Free (Tenryu-ji garden ~¥500)<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Arashiyama%20Bamboo%20Grove">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbaT9dGywsB/">@giashn</a> – Arashiyama day: Sagano Romantic Train + Hozugawa boat + bamboo<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bamboo_Forest_(Kyoto)">Bamboo Forest (Kyoto) (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.6717,35.017,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D5.6 Adashino Nenbutsu-ji and its quiet bamboo path</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>15:05–16:00</b> Adashino Nenbutsu-ji and its quiet bamboo path<br>Cost: ~¥500<br><b>⚠ Last entry 16:00 (16:30 close). Don't linger at lunch.</b><br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Adashino%20Nenbutsu-ji">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adashino_Nenbutsu-ji">Adashino Nenbutsu-ji (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.6667,35.0247,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D5.7 Togetsukyo bridge at sunset</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>16:20–17:00</b> Togetsukyo bridge at sunset (≈ 16:47)<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Togetsukyo%20Bridge%2C%20Kyoto">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DeOD8Tzks5Q/">@photo post</a> – Best autumn-leaf spots in Japan, incl. Arashiyama and Eikando<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbaT9dGywsB/">@giashn</a> – Arashiyama day: Sagano Romantic Train + Hozugawa boat + bamboo<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arashiyama">Arashiyama (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.6779,35.013,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D5.8 Evening</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>18:00–20:00</b> Evening: Nishiki area / Pontocho dinner (if moved from Day 4)<br>Kinkaku-ji closes at 17:00, so it doesn't fit today. It's on tomorrow morning.<br>Cost: You pay: dinner<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nishiki%20Market%2C%20Kyoto">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nishiki_Market">Nishiki Market (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.765,35.005,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 5 route</name><styleUrl>#d4</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Torokko%20Saga%20Station%2C%20Kyoto/Torokko%20Kameoka%20Station/Hozugawa%20River%20Boat%20Ride%2C%20Kameoka/Kumonocha%20Cafe%20Arashiyama/Arashiyama%20Bamboo%20Grove/Adashino%20Nenbutsu-ji/Togetsukyo%20Bridge%2C%20Kyoto/Nishiki%20Market%2C%20Kyoto">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>135.6815,35.018,0 135.6063,35.0198,0 135.5862,35.0128,0 135.6772,35.015,0 135.6717,35.017,0 135.6667,35.0247,0 135.6779,35.013,0 135.765,35.005,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 6 · Mon 30 Nov · Kinkaku-ji → Tokyo</name>
<Placemark><name>D6.1 Kinkaku-ji</name><styleUrl>#d5</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>09:00–09:50</b> Kinkaku-ji, the Golden Pavilion, at opening<br>Cost: ~¥500<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kinkaku-ji">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinkaku-ji">Kinkaku-ji (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.7292,35.0394,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D6.2 Kyoto station</name><styleUrl>#d5</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>10:30–11:09</b> Kyoto station: bento for the train<br>Cost: You pay: lunch<br><b>⚠ If Kinkaku-ji runs late, take a later Nozomi; they run every 10 min. Just keep the Shibuya Sky slot in mind.</b><br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kyoto%20Station">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dep4Xv2IPc3/">@tyler.travelssmart</a> – Train money tips: Tokyo 72 h subway ticket, local train Osaka–Kyoto, skip the JR Pass<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ky%C5%8Dto_Station">Kyōto Station (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.7588,34.9858,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D6.3 Drop bags</name><styleUrl>#d5</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>13:45–14:50</b> Drop bags, Comfort Hotel Tokyo Higashi Nihombashi<br>Cost: In package, with breakfast<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Comfort%20Hotel%20Tokyo%20Higashi%20Nihombashi">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi">Nihonbashi (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7843,35.6922,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D6.4 Shibuya Sky</name><styleUrl>#d5</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>15:40–17:00</b> Shibuya Sky, sunset slot (sunset ≈ 16:28) + Scramble Crossing<br>Cost: In package<br><b>⚠ Fixed time slot. This is the third timed thing today after Kinkaku-ji and the Shinkansen.</b><br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shibuya%20Sky">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXeqhI1gFl3/">@mr.jodigo</a> – Japan shopping haul: Kappabashi knife (Musashi), Haruta loafers, Shibuya Scramble shops<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shibuya_Scramble_Square">Shibuya Scramble Square (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7022,35.6585,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D6.5 Sumo live show with photo</name><styleUrl>#d5</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>18:00–19:30</b> Sumo live show with photo, Shinjuku<br>Cost: In package<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kabukicho%2C%20Shinjuku">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumo">Sumo (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.702,35.695,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D6.6 Dinner</name><styleUrl>#d5</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>19:45–21:00</b> Dinner: Digiro digital sushi or Omoide Yokocho<br>Cost: You pay: dinner<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Omoide%20Yokocho%2C%20Shinjuku">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcoURkphxRj/">@tabibiyori.travelsupport</a> – Free things: Jihanpi drinks app, Toyosu rooftop footbath, Digiro digital sushi in Shinjuku<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DY7j8MwxE_o/">@her.atlas</a> – JINS Shinjuku: eye test and glasses in 30 minutes<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabukich%C5%8D">Kabukichō (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7006,35.6896,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 6 route</name><styleUrl>#d5</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Kinkaku-ji/Kyoto%20Station/Comfort%20Hotel%20Tokyo%20Higashi%20Nihombashi/Shibuya%20Sky/Kabukicho%2C%20Shinjuku/Omoide%20Yokocho%2C%20Shinjuku">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>135.7292,35.0394,0 135.7588,34.9858,0 139.7843,35.6922,0 139.7022,35.6585,0 139.702,35.695,0 139.7006,35.6896,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 7 · Tue 1 Dec · Asakusa + Toyosu</name>
<Placemark><name>D7.1+3 Benitsuru</name><styleUrl>#d6</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>06:50–07:15</b> Benitsuru: queue for a soufflé pancake ticket<br>Bring ¥1,000 cash deposit per pancake; you get a time slot for later.<br>Cost: You pay: cash deposit<br><br><b>09:00–10:00</b> Pancake slot at Benitsuru (time depends on your ticket)<br>Cost: You pay: ~¥1,800 per pancake<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Benitsuru%2C%20Asakusa">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DefwRUry65P/">@kyleandmiyu</a> – Benitsuru soufflé pancakes, Asakusa (ticket queue ~6:30am, ¥1,000 cash deposit)<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asakusa">Asakusa (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7958,35.7122,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D7.2 Senso-ji while it's still quiet</name><styleUrl>#d6</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>07:20–08:30</b> Senso-ji while it's still quiet<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Senso-ji%2C%20Asakusa">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sens%C5%8D-ji">Sensō-ji (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7967,35.7148,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D7.4 Asakusa street food crawl</name><styleUrl>#d6</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>10:00–12:00</b> Asakusa street food crawl<br>Age.3 sandos, Hokkaido Milk Bar, Ginkado mochi, Anshinya chicken, Kagetsudo melon pan. Most are under ¥1,000.<br>Cost: You pay: snacks<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nakamise%20Shopping%20Street%2C%20Asakusa">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdKDfvGMuc7/">@travelwithudita</a> – Asakusa viral street food under ¥1,000<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcCY-QOPNlr/">@jessiejanedaye</a> – Food worth the hype: Kumonocha cloud matcha, Age.3 sandos, Hiiragi shaved ice<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sens%C5%8D-ji">Sensō-ji (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7963,35.7118,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D7.5 Kappabashi kitchen street</name><styleUrl>#d6</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>12:15–13:30</b> Kappabashi kitchen street: knives (pack in checked luggage)<br>Cost: Free to browse<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kappabashi%20Dougu%20Street">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXeqhI1gFl3/">@mr.jodigo</a> – Japan shopping haul: Kappabashi knife (Musashi), Haruta loafers, Shibuya Scramble shops<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kappabashi-dori">Kappabashi-dori (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.788,35.7135,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D7.6+7 Late lunch</name><styleUrl>#d6</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>14:15–15:00</b> Late lunch, Senkyaku Banrai food hall<br>Cost: You pay: lunch<br><br><b>15:00–16:40</b> Free rooftop footbath, sunset over Tokyo Bay (≈ 16:28)<br>Bring a small towel.<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Toyosu%20Senkyaku%20Banrai">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcoURkphxRj/">@tabibiyori.travelsupport</a> – Free things: Jihanpi drinks app, Toyosu rooftop footbath, Digiro digital sushi in Shinjuku<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyosu_Market">Toyosu Market (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7845,35.6455,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D7.8 teamLab Planets</name><styleUrl>#d6</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>17:00–19:00</b> teamLab Planets (book the 17:00 slot)<br>Swapped with the footbath so you get the sunset from the roof.<br>Cost: In package<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=teamLab%20Planets%20TOKYO">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyosu">Toyosu (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7898,35.6491,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D7.9 Ginza dinner + Hiiragi shaved ice; Uniqlo / Onitsuka Tiger flagships</name><styleUrl>#d6</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>19:30–21:30</b> Ginza dinner + Hiiragi shaved ice; Uniqlo / Onitsuka Tiger flagships<br>Cost: You pay: dinner, shopping<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ginza%2C%20Tokyo">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcCY-QOPNlr/">@jessiejanedaye</a> – Food worth the hype: Kumonocha cloud matcha, Age.3 sandos, Hiiragi shaved ice<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginza">Ginza (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.765,35.6717,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 7 route</name><styleUrl>#d6</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Benitsuru%2C%20Asakusa/Senso-ji%2C%20Asakusa/Benitsuru%2C%20Asakusa/Nakamise%20Shopping%20Street%2C%20Asakusa/Kappabashi%20Dougu%20Street/Toyosu%20Senkyaku%20Banrai/teamLab%20Planets%20TOKYO/Ginza%2C%20Tokyo">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>139.7958,35.7122,0 139.7967,35.7148,0 139.7958,35.7122,0 139.7963,35.7118,0 139.788,35.7135,0 139.7845,35.6455,0 139.7898,35.6491,0 139.765,35.6717,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 8 · Wed 2 Dec · Fuji · ryokan night</name>
<Placemark><name>D8.1 Chureito Pagoda</name><styleUrl>#d7</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>10:30–12:00</b> Chureito Pagoda (398 steps), Fuji views clearest in the morning<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Chureito%20Pagoda">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arakurayama_Sengen_Park">Arakurayama Sengen Park (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.8017,35.5013,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D8.2 Lunch</name><styleUrl>#d7</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>12:30–13:45</b> Lunch: hoto noodles; drop bags at the ryokan<br>Cost: You pay: lunch<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kawaguchiko%20Station">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Kawaguchi">Lake Kawaguchi (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.7686,35.4979,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D8.3 Oishi Park + Momiji maple corridor</name><styleUrl>#d7</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>14:15–16:40</b> Oishi Park + Momiji maple corridor, sunset over the lake<br>Cost: Free<br><b>⚠ Maples may be just past peak by 2 Dec. The Fuji view is the reason to go.</b><br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Oishi%20Park%2C%20Fujikawaguchiko">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Fuji">Mount Fuji (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.7522,35.5196,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D8.4 Ryokan</name><styleUrl>#d7</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>17:15–22:00</b> Ryokan: private onsen, kaiseki dinner<br>If the ryokan has no good bath, Fujiyama Onsen (from the reel) is 15 min by taxi, ~¥1,800.<br>Cost: Not in quote: ~¥40,000–80,000 per room, dinner + breakfast<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=35.51%2C138.768">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryokan">Ryokan (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.768,35.51,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 8 route</name><styleUrl>#d7</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Chureito%20Pagoda/Kawaguchiko%20Station/Oishi%20Park%2C%20Fujikawaguchiko/35.51%2C138.768">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>138.8017,35.5013,0 138.7686,35.4979,0 138.7522,35.5196,0 138.768,35.51,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 9 · Thu 3 Dec · Shiraito Falls → Tokyo</name>
<Placemark><name>D9.1 Sunrise Fuji view</name><styleUrl>#d8</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>06:30–08:30</b> Sunrise Fuji view, onsen, breakfast<br>Cost: Part of the ryokan stay<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=35.51%2C138.768">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryokan">Ryokan (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.768,35.51,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D9.2 Shiraito Falls + Otodome Falls</name><styleUrl>#d8</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>09:30–10:45</b> Shiraito Falls + Otodome Falls<br>Cost: Free<br><b>⚠ Not enough time by public transport: it's 2.5+ hours with 3 changes each way. Only do this with a car booked for the whole leg. Without a car, skip it and spend the morning around Lake Kawaguchi.</b><br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shiraito%20Falls%2C%20Fujinomiya">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcNyyJaM-DU/">@saltinourhair</a> – Shiraito Falls with Mt Fuji behind<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiraito_Falls">Shiraito Falls (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.5871,35.3124,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D9.3 Back at the Tokyo hotel</name><styleUrl>#d8</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>13:30–14:15</b> Back at the Tokyo hotel<br>Cost: In package, with breakfast<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Comfort%20Hotel%20Tokyo%20Higashi%20Nihombashi">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi">Nihonbashi (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7843,35.6922,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D9.4 Harajuku</name><styleUrl>#d8</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>14:45–18:30</b> Harajuku, Omotesando shopping; Regetta shoes, Don Quijote<br>Cost: You pay: shopping<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Omotesando%2C%20Tokyo">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcsKqOnBPNn/">@Hemani &amp; Sagar</a> – Regetta walking shoes instead of Onitsuka Tiger<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harajuku">Harajuku (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7027,35.6702,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D9.5 Shinjuku evening</name><styleUrl>#d8</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>19:00–21:00</b> Shinjuku evening, dinner<br>Cost: You pay: dinner<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Omoide%20Yokocho%2C%20Shinjuku">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcoURkphxRj/">@tabibiyori.travelsupport</a> – Free things: Jihanpi drinks app, Toyosu rooftop footbath, Digiro digital sushi in Shinjuku<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DY7j8MwxE_o/">@her.atlas</a> – JINS Shinjuku: eye test and glasses in 30 minutes<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabukich%C5%8D">Kabukichō (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7006,35.6896,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Day 9 route</name><styleUrl>#d8</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Straight lines between stops, in order. Directions: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/35.51%2C138.768/Shiraito%20Falls%2C%20Fujinomiya/Comfort%20Hotel%20Tokyo%20Higashi%20Nihombashi/Omotesando%2C%20Tokyo/Omoide%20Yokocho%2C%20Shinjuku">open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>138.768,35.51,0 138.5871,35.3124,0 139.7843,35.6922,0 139.7027,35.6702,0 139.7006,35.6896,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 10 · Fri 4 Dec · DisneySea</name>
<Placemark><name>D10.1 Tokyo DisneySea</name><styleUrl>#d9</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>08:30–21:00</b> Tokyo DisneySea<br>Be at the gate 30 min before opening. Premier Access for Fantasy Springs rides is bought in the app.<br>Cost: Ticket in package; Premier Access ~¥1,500–2,500 per ride extra<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tokyo%20DisneySea">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo_DisneySea">Tokyo DisneySea (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.8851,35.6267,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 11 · Sat 5 Dec · Kamakura + Enoshima (only with 3rd extra day)</name>
<Placemark><name>D11.1 Tsurugaoka Hachimangu</name><styleUrl>#d10</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>09:00–10:15</b> Tsurugaoka Hachimangu<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tsurugaoka%20Hachimangu">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsurugaoka_Hachimang%C5%AB">Tsurugaoka Hachimangū (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.5564,35.3259,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D11.2 Komachi-dori street snacks</name><styleUrl>#d10</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>10:15–11:00</b> Komachi-dori street snacks<br>Cost: You pay: snacks<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Komachi-dori%2C%20Kamakura">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kamakura">Kamakura (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.5503,35.319,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D11.3 Great Buddha</name><styleUrl>#d10</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>11:15–12:00</b> Great Buddha, Kotoku-in<br>Cost: ~¥300<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kotoku-in%20Great%20Buddha%20of%20Kamakura">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K%C5%8Dtoku-in">Kōtoku-in (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.5359,35.3167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D11.4 Hase-dera</name><styleUrl>#d10</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>12:05–13:30</b> Hase-dera (early-Dec maples) + lunch with sea view<br>Cost: ~¥400 + lunch<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hase-dera%20Kamakura">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hase-dera_(Kamakura)">Hase-dera (Kamakura) (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.5334,35.3127,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D11.5 The level crossing by the sea</name><styleUrl>#d10</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>13:45–14:15</b> The level crossing by the sea<br>Cost: Free<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kamakurakokomae%20Station">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdqpJDkMYyF/">@pathandpassports</a> – 10-day route: Asakusa, Kawaguchiko, Kyoto list, Nara, Kamakura + Enoden<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enoshima_Electric_Railway">Enoshima Electric Railway (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.5004,35.3067,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D11.6 Enoshima island</name><styleUrl>#d10</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>14:45–17:00</b> Enoshima island, Sea Candle at sunset (≈ 16:28)<br>Cost: ~¥1,100 garden + tower<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Enoshima%20Sea%20Candle">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enoshima">Enoshima (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.4806,35.2994,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>D11.7 Last-night dinner; snacks for home</name><styleUrl>#d10</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>18:30–21:00</b> Last-night dinner; snacks for home (KitKats, Royce, Black Thunder)<br>Cost: You pay: dinner, snacks<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Omoide%20Yokocho%2C%20Shinjuku">Open in Google Maps</a><br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcoURkphxRj/">@tabibiyori.travelsupport</a> – Free things: Jihanpi drinks app, Toyosu rooftop footbath, Digiro digital sushi in Shinjuku<br>Your reel: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DY7j8MwxE_o/">@her.atlas</a> – JINS Shinjuku: eye test and glasses in 30 minutes<br>Photo: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabukich%C5%8D">Kabukichō (Wikipedia)</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.7006,35.6896,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
